WEBVTT

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.100
Let's start!

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.850
We had entered the main computer and were cornered by the drones...

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:10.560
!olleH

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.130
...but with the guidance of Tako, a robot Adam's parents had left behind...

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:20.400
...we were able to escape to a hidden area Survive's control wouldn't reach.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:27.660
Then, while gathering food in preparation for our showdown with Survive...

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.430
...we reunited with Sharla and Howard, who we had thought lost.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:42.000
Sharla and Howard had been carried here by an underground aqueduct below the desert.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:05.360
Very well.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:08.290
We shall continue observing Luna.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:18.000
What's wrong?

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.500
Drones.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.290
Which way?

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:21.710
This way, I think.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:22.880
Damn it!

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.300
What's wrong?

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.550
Sharla went to look for food!

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.530
Sharla!

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.730
Sharla...

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.080
Sharla!

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.060
She's not here.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.190
Don't tell me the drones...

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.990
Sharla... Sharla!

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.450
What a relief! You're safe!

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:56.960
Are you okay?

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:02.340
Yes, but... what's wrong? You both seem so worried.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.760
Luna sensed the presence of the drones.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.260
It's dangerous to stay here too long. Let's go back to the hidden area.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:11.820
Yes.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.390
I have to admit, it's an amazing security system.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.890
That's because you're not as smart as I!

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.440
Whaddaya expect to get outta braggin'?

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.200
It's the truth!

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:39.830
That was fast.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:41.440
The drones were there.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.510
But you were okay, right?

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.400
Yes, I only sensed their presence.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:01.430
A real amazin' bunch. I'd'a thought they'd'a given up by now. Right?

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:02.660
Yes.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.800
How were things on your end?

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:09.230
We gave up. We can't make contact with Survive from here.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.530
It looks like we'll have to go to the main room.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.090
Main room?

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:14.930
'At's right

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.040
Right here.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.680
This whole spaceship is controlled from here.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.260
Put another way, it's Survive's heart.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:26.480
The room where Survive itself is.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.910
The room where Survive itself is...

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.700
Incidentally, the hidden area where we are is here.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.200
They're pretty far apart.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.790
But that's not all.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:55.240
This is the network system diagram for this place.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:58.580
I just recently opened a connection and discovered it.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.910
What would happen if it were traced?

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:02.850
Nothin' to worry 'bout.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.060
We hid the connection source.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.840
It should think it's just a regular transmission.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.790
Well okay then...

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:13.890
The sensors and drones in each block are connected...

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.810
...so the information received about intruders...

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:20.780
...is transmitted to the other security drones.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.310
Is it transmitted to Survive too?

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:27.560
No, the sensors are isolated from the main system.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:33.110
When there's an intruder, the drones can take care of it, so Survive doesn't need to be told.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.180
So don't worry on that count.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:41.660
But, we'll have to do something about the sensors and drones, or we won't make it to the main room.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:46.420
If we can just do something about the drones, I think I can handle the sensors.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:49.950
So we need a way to drive the drones away.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.940
Why're you imitatin' 'em?

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:02.180
That's it!

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:03.680
What is it, all of a sudden?

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:09.780
I just remembered that the drones have a simple maintenance ability.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.660
Maintenance ability?

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:16.690
Yes, the ability to repair damage that occurs within their block.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:23.750
If we send a false damage signal from here, we may be able to mislead the drones!

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:26.000
Can we send a signal like that?

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.050
Please leave it to me!

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:35.100
Of course, to send a signal will require me to open a connection, but I'll make it untraceable!

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:36.560
That's amazing, Tako!

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.430
No, not so much...

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:41.250
What do you mean, not so much?

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:44.640
You forgot about their maintenance ability, didn't'cha?

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.580
Wait for it, Survive!

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:50.150
When we make it to the main room, we'll shut you down right away!

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.600
Shut down?

00:07:56.290 --> 00:08:00.200
Wat a second! By shut down, you mean to turn off Survive?

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:02.060
Luna?

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:05.850
Do we really need to turn Survive off?

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.130
As long as we get the space ship, that's enough for us...

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:14.010
That may be true, but without turning Survive off, we won't be able to get the space ship.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:17.660
No, if we discuss it we might come to an understanding.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.130
I'm not so sure.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.340
Have you forgotten?

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:24.140
Survive says people are unnecessary.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:25.280
That's right!

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.710
He's trying to kill us!

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.180
I realize that.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:30.680
But...

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.240
Survive, tell me!

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.330
What should we do?

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:43.950
Survive!

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:53.930
I want to talk with him more.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:55.260
I mean, at this rate...

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:57.110
I agree with Luna.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.480
We don't have to shut him down or anything.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.220
I want to try talking to Survive too.

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:03.490
Sharla!

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.230
I agree with Luna too.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:12.770
What's goin' on? Up 'til now we were always about breakin' Survive and takin' the ship.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:16.280
Anyways, I'm against shutting Survive down.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.890
In any event, if we can't make contact with Survive, none of that matters.

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:24.260
Let's think about making it to the main room for now.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.330
Let's get to plannin' the operation!

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.460
Well, off we go.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:44.780
Don't press your luck.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:48.860
As much as we talked about drawing the drones away, we're using a fake signal.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.190
We don't know how well it will work.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:52.050
Right.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:52.990
Luna...

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.650
Don't worry, I'm sure it will go well.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.460
Well, we're countin' on ya!

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.530
Leave it to me!

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:01.880
Let's go.

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:06.710
We should make ready as well.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:07.800
Yes!

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:33.640
It's the drones.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.800
That's the network node, I suppose.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.640
A'ight, let's get started.

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:53.250
Okay.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:54.450
Let's start.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:55.910
Roger that.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.330
Transmitting damage signal.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:05.930
Finished.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.100
Closing connection.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:18.410
Looks like it worked.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.860
They won't come back, right?

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:29.780
It went okay.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:31.130
Right, let's go too!

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:42.450
This, 'n that, 'n then...

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:48.230
Chako!

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:49.460
I know!

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.530
Now, Shingo!

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:17.360
With that, the sensor change is finished.

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:21.450
As long as the drones don't realize, this place is the same as the hidden area.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:24.190
Yeah, yeah. Let this take care of the rest.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:28.910
They did it.

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:30.150
Yes!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:33.900
Luna!

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:35.060
Alright, the next one.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.600
Roger!

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:15.020
We made it.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.750
Alright, A-2 block secured.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:22.840
Next one.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:23.850
Roger!

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:05.740
Now the C block is secured too.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.430
All that's left is D block.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:09.790
What was that just now?

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.160
A strange reaction in A-1 block.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:14.850
A strange reaction?

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:16.850
I don't notice anything.

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.440
That's not true! I'm sure just now in A-1 Block...

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:24.110
We might have been found out by the drones.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.170
I'll take a look.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:28.650
Be careful.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:32.810
But nothing's wrong.

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:51.260
Looks like nothing out of the ordinary.

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:54.410
Maybe I just imagined it after all.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:55.990
I'm sorry.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.980
Let's continue as planned.

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.180
Roger!

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:11.550
Luna...

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:22.990
A little longer...

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:25.610
But who'd have thought it would go this easily?

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:29.100
Now it's just a matter of time before we reach the main room.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:32.480
They're coming.

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:34.580
What?

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:54.190
That was a close call.

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:57.490
But why did it come back so quickly?

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.260
More are coming.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.650
That Tako screwed up!

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:05.630
There they are!

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.150
What's wrong?

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:09.900
Aye.

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:15.900
Luna!

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.660
Let's hide over there.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:36.080
They're gone.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:41.850
The sensors aren't working, so as long as we dodge the drones we'll be fine!

00:16:57.940 --> 00:16:58.650
Let's go.

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:03.600
They're back!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:11.930
Luna...

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:21.010
The mod chips are breaking!

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:23.330
Looks like Survive noticed.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:47.180
Luna!

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:53.140
Look out!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:03.040
That was close.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.380
Thank you, Adam.

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:09.490
C'mon, let's go.

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.960
Damn it!

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:21.260
Everyone, a little further!

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.740
Everyone, are you okay?

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:36.980
Somehow.

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:38.180
Me too.

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:39.300
Me too.

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:43.990
Looks like they're tryin' to get in here.

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:47.360
Let's go back for a while and regroup.

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:48.260
Good idea.

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:53.850
Luna!

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:00.000
Luna, were you okay?

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:01.280
Thanks, Adam.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.490
We made it thanks to you.

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:05.060
What a relief!

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:07.050
Damn it, Tako!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.580
How couldja screw up at such an important time?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:10.910
I didn't...

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:11.850
Idiot!

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:14.060
What didn't you what?

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:16.460
Makin' excuses, even though you're a robot!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.110
But I didn't...

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:19.880
Shut up!

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.880
Stop it, the two of you!

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:24.340
This is no time to be fighting!

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:25.690
But...

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:27.150
That's right!

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:31.240
If we don't think up some countermeasure, the drones will head here!

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:32.770
What? The drones?

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:33.710
That's right.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:37.580
Chako, Tako, check the system one more time with Shingo.

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.980
There must be something we can do.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:41.060
Yes!

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:43.730
We'll search for weapons.

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:45.380
Okay.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:49.430
What's this?

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:51.380
Looks like a transmission record.

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:56.210
This is strange. I don't remember transmitting this signal.

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:03.000
A-1 Block, A-1 Block...

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:06.080
What?

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:10.280
Luna... Luna!

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:12.940
C'mere for a sec.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:23.360
Howard is linked to Survive?

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:26.250
No doubt about it. Probably Sharla too.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:28.350
I thought it was strange.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:31.160
For them to survive being swallowed up in quicksand like that.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:34.310
But to think Sharla and Howard...

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:47.590
Everyone, we've found our next plan!

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:49.050
Really?

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:54.150
We found a program unit in the system that's not currently being used.

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:57.860
If we use it, we can invade Survive, even from here.

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:00.150
We can shut him down!

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:05.100
Alright, get started as soon as you can.

00:21:05.440 --> 00:21:06.600
Leave it to us!

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:09.900
...or so I'd like to say, but first we chow down!

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.290
Chow down?

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.210
It looks like there's a lotta work ahead.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:17.060
You can't fight on an empty stomach!

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:23.850
Everyone go on and eat ahead of me.

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:26.250
I'll keep watch here.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:28.390
Sorry. We'll be back soon.

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:31.880
Where's Luna?

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:35.030
You shouldn't ask where a lady's gone.

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:06.150
Program Unit... Program Unit...

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:07.840
Where is it?

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:09.560
What are you doing?

00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:15.980
Sharla... You really are...

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:18.340
You tricked me.

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:19.760
Howard!

00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:23.890
Howard?

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:28.460
Sharla, please!

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:28.990
Let go!

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:29.890
Where's the old Sharla?

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:34.610
This way.

00:22:41.930 --> 00:22:43.240
Sharla! Howard!

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:46.580
What's wrong?

00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:47.660
Howard...

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:05.180
Howard and Sharla are Survive's spies?

00:23:05.590 --> 00:23:07.280
Why would it do something like that?

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:11.060
Maybe it's trying to investigate the mysterious power you have, Luna.

00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:16.540
My power? I don't know what meaning it holds for Survive.

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:23.030
But more than anything, those two are important to me! I'll definitely take them back from Survive!

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:27.600
Next time: You're your own person.
